g  execution and progress etc  and they also had reports on issues and  deviations as one of their key  functions that they wanted the software  to have  additional benefits to paperless  validation include  streamlining your metrics and and having  data mining  expediting your protocol generation and  execution  improved response time during audits for  retrieval of packages  real-time review and monitoring of tasks  for validation  reducing your documentation errors  reducing the use of office supplies such  as paper and printer  toner cartridge and binders eliminating  the documentation  transportation and storage in your  validation library as well as your  validation librarian  and it maintains the order and  relationship of documents  the director of i.t quality at the  pharmaceutical company i spoke with  she said that by instituting a paperless  validation solution it allows them to  focus  on the actual work of validation  eliminating the manual labor related to  the workflow  and document management validation  personnel can  fully focus on the actual job of doing  the validation planning it  specifications testing and reporting  this facilitates compliance and reduces  the cost and cycle time for validation  overall  so software options i'm going to present  three that i reviewed  and looked for uh five validation has a  product called go5  neat solutions and val genesis  we'll take a look at each one one at a  time so five validation has a product  called go5  they were founded in 2019 and launched  their validation software the same year  gopher five validation is a validation  company that has developed their own  software for managing validation  paperwork  they in turn use their validation  software at their clients that  contract with them for validation work  and they use it for free just to show  them and test it out if the client is  willing  so they can see what paperless  validation might look like and whether  it's something that they would li